{"id": "EUVD-2026-103615", "enisaUuid": "9a56ad24-d0b7-30ad-be11-9b41d1920c6b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: ipv6: keep room for the mac header in dst_dev_overhead()\n\nThe seg6, ioam6 and rpl lwtunnels size their skb_cow_head() request as\nthe length they are about to push plus dst_dev_overhead(), then push the\nnew headers and rebuild the mac header below them with\nskb_mac_header_rebuild().  That rebuild needs skb->mac_len of headroom,\nbut dst_dev_overhead() leaves LL_RESERVED_SPACE() of the egress device,\n16 bytes for plain Ethernet.\n\nWhere the mac header is longer than that, as it is on ingress through a\nVLAN device with reorder_hdr off, the rebuild runs out of room:\nskb_set_mac_header(skb, -skb->mac_len) computes a negative offset,\nstores it unchecked in the u16 skb->mac_header, and the memmove that\nfollows writes skb->mac_len bytes about 64 KB past skb->head.\nForwarding plain ping6 traffic through such a device reproduces it on\nall five seg6 encapsulation modes and on the rpl and ioam6 inline paths;\nskb->mac_header comes back as 65534 on a 704-byte head.\n\nReturn the larger of the two.  The helper already returns skb->mac_len\nwhen it has no dst, so this only makes the other branch agree, and it\ncovers every caller rather than each call site in turn.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:18:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:55", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36c07127924f11fc5741a780abcaaf808fe9ef13", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/87cd6b717e4069dca34e0866e57eaeb44d3b173e"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98570", "GHSA-4prh-wfp5-28j7"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "056eaf5e-1ecc-3a3e-8471-8cf62054130d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b26f015dfb07b6be12d005a0ed0c5c43b7bedbf3"}, {"id": "095a0e17-3f95-337a-92bc-7aef841fcef2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4a855c5aec41bf84922224ab7a74e088776e3ac4"}, {"id": "329f6ce2-efb1-390b-8356-6745a0acfd1d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4c12c3c8abd8b888945d31e7bdbb0d8b73032fc5"}, {"id": "336ce968-1aa1-362b-9ffa-a5788c859915", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "36da2b2b-30f4-3883-bf91-7ea4944d550a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15.179 <5.16"}, {"id": "767ceb45-4511-3a1e-ae2e-abd7d713f417", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "25d8e065c7972dc98fd7a4cac322d5367eaede88"}, {"id": "78c0f76b-fde9-38f8-9b70-88283d1dc128", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10.235 <5.11"}, {"id": "7c934acc-f6e2-3ea2-b69f-bbd12fca30d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.14"}, {"id": "86440bce-c105-35d5-b43f-46f4dd2313ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2fcc9f3798ef82399564d247458e69abd10e683b"}, {"id": "89fb55c7-4454-30fc-bbf4-b827c2c0a96e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1.130 <6.2"}, {"id": "91575396-ba35-3748-b351-94041ce96c88", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ab9de9c48316d2622d3bf353916b99971570e2c9"}, {"id": "92673dbc-332a-3f6a-9d70-dbe647b5d866", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "634710a372ba65bee667c2f6e58a97658c639eab"}, {"id": "93c5d479-126d-374d-a42f-9c83702adff9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "94ad147c-61a8-3181-b4de-d21829154476", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.13.4 <6.14"}, {"id": "a781f2d1-c188-3716-b1b5-a67b7a266a71", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "